{
  "schema": "sa2-recomp-handle-regions/v1",
  "about": [
    "Every range of synthetic values this runtime hands the guest: handles",
    "outside the guest address space, synthetic COM objects and vtables inside",
    "it, and the thunk regions imports and interface methods are dispatched on.",
    "",
    "They must not overlap. Two kinds sharing a range means a value of the",
    "wrong kind is a plausible one rather than a recognisable one, which is",
    "exactly what each of these regions exists to prevent. On 2026-09-21 the",
    "first open file handle and the first window handle were bit-identical",
    "because SA2_VFS_HANDLE_BASE and SA2_WND_HWND_BASE were both 0x7e000000,",
    "and the collision was found by a unit adding a fourth set of tokens, not",
    "by anything looking for it.",
    "",
    "Checked by Documentation/scripts/check_handle_regions.py, which reads each",
    "constant out of its header so a moved constant cannot pass, and fails on",
    "any *_BASE in the handle space that is not declared here."
  ],
  "regions": [
    {
      "name": "SteamMetricsSDK MetricsAgent token",
      "header": "runtime/sa2_iface.c",
      "base": "SA2_METRICS_AGENT_TOKEN",
      "stride": 16,
      "count": 1,
      "space": "handle",
      "note": "One value, not a range: MetricsAgent is a singleton and GetInstance always answers the same token. It is declared anyway so that nothing else can be placed on it, which is the whole point of the undeclared-base clause."
    },
    {
      "name": "VFS file and find handles",
      "header": "runtime/sa2_files.h",
      "base": "SA2_VFS_HANDLE_BASE",
      "stride": "SA2_VFS_HANDLE_STRIDE",
      "count": "SA2_VFS_HANDLE_MAX",
      "space": "handle"
    },
    {
